{"last_link_id": 805, "nodes": [{"mode": 0, "showAdvanced": true, "outputs": [{"name": "width", "links": [784], "label": "width", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "width"}, {"name": "height", "links": [785], "label": "height", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "height"}], "size": [306.9424133300781, 150], "pos": [233.03550720214844, 3476.771240234375], "widgets_values": ["9:16 (Portrait Widescreen)", 1, 32], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "preview", "label": "preview", "type": "RESOLUTION_PREVIEW", "localized_name": "preview"}, {"widget": {"name": "aspect_ratio"}, "name": "aspect_ratio", "label": "aspect_ratio", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "aspect_ratio"}, {"widget": {"name": "megapixels"}, "name": "megapixels", "label": "megapixels", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "megapixels"}, {"widget": {"name": "multiple"}, "name": "multiple", "label": "multiple", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "multiple"}], "flags": {}, "id": 13, "type": "ResolutionSelector", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.37.0", "widget_ue_connectable": {"aspect_ratio": true, "megapixels": true, "multiple": true}, "Node name for S&R": "ResolutionSelector"}, "order": 0}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["## Size\nQwen Image 2.1 has native 2K (2048*2048) support for direct output.\n\n- resolution is a total pixel budget (not width or height). Aspect ratio is preserved.\n- Official default is 1024. The model supports up to 2048.\n- This template starts at 0: no resize beyond a multiple of 32.\n- Output follows image_1. Extra refs can differ in size or aspect.\n- custom_size off: canvas comes from the encode latent (image_1).\n- custom_size on: use ResolutionSelector width/height. Keep it close to the resized image_1 size, or the edit can shift.\n\n## Reference images\n- Up to 10 reference images (image_1 to image_10).\n- Mention them in the prompt as `<image1>`, `<image2>`, ...\n- image_1 is the edit target. The rest are references.\n\n## Custom settings\nIf you need custom settings, enter or unpack the subgraph to edit it. See the [Subgraph](https://docs.comfy.org/interface/features/subgraph) guide.\n\n## Parameters\n- prompt: edit instruction. Use `<image1>` ... `<image10>`.\n- negative_prompt: unused while cfg is 1.\n- cfg: keep 1 for the Qwen Image 2.1 official path. Raise it only if you use a negative prompt.\n- steps: Qwen Image 2.1 official pipeline uses about 40-50 with euler. This template starts at 25. More advanced samplers need fewer steps."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Note: Usage", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#000", "size": [420, 620], "pos": [-715.0750732421875, 2533.0732421875], "id": 463, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 1}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["## Qwen-Image 2.1 - Image Edit + Turbo (4-6 Steps)\n\n[Qwen-Image 2.1](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1) is Qwen's unified text-to-image + image-editing model (7B visual component). This workflow is the **image-edit** side with a **community turbo LoRA** wired in, so edits finish in **4-6 steps** at cfg 1 instead of 20+.\n\nBased on the official ComfyUI Qwen-Image 2.1 edit workflow, with a **GGUF loader path** for lower-VRAM cards, the turbo LoRA slot, and an image-comparer. Toggle paths with the Fast Groups Bypasser.\n\n### Turbo LoRAs (pick one - loaded in the LoRA slot)\n- [Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo-v0.2.1-6step-lora-r256.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Viggle/Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo/tree/main) -> `models/loras/` -- **6-step, loaded by default here.** By Viggle.\n- [Qwen-Image-2.1-Fun-Acc-4Step.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/alibaba-pai/Qwen-Image-2.1-Fun-Acc-LoRAs/tree/main/models) -> `models/loras/` -- **4-step alternate.** By Alibaba-PAI. Drop KSampler to 4 steps when you swap to this one.\n\nBoth run at cfg 1, sampler er_sde (euler also works), scheduler simple, LoRA strength 1.0.\n\n### IMPORTANT - turbo caution (read this)\nThese turbo LoRAs are **consistently great for image editing** (the job of this workflow). But **text-to-image on the turbo LoRAs is hit-or-miss** -- some prompts come out clean, others come out **incomplete or smeared**. This was the same on **both** LoRAs in testing; cause is unknown, hopefully the creators tighten it up. So:\n- Use turbo for **editing** here, where it's reliable.\n- For dependable **text-to-image**, use the standard (non-turbo) Qwen-Image 2.1 model at full steps.\n\n### Base models\nSame as the non-turbo edit workflow:\n- [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/diffusion_models) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (~7 GB, default)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_Q5_K_M.gguf](https://huggingface.co/Abiray/Qwen-Image-2.1-GGUF/tree/main) (or another quant, ~4-7 GB) -> `models/unet/` (low VRAM)\n- [qwen3vl_8b_w4a8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/`\n- [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/` (alternate encoder)\n- [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/tree/main/vae) -> `models/vae/`\n\nTurbo LoRAs by **Viggle** and **Alibaba-PAI** -- credit to both. Read each model card for license/terms."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Note: Model links", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#000", "size": [420, 620], "pos": [-713.167236328125, 3201.912841796875], "id": 476, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 2}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "MODEL", "links": [781], "label": "MODEL", "type": "MODEL", "localized_name": "MODEL"}], "size": [270, 90], "pos": [1470.0101318359375, 2598.976806640625], "widgets_values": ["auto", "default"], "inputs": [{"name": "model", "link": 797, "label": "model", "type": "MODEL", "localized_name": "model"}, {"widget": {"name": "device"}, "name": "device", "label": "